    "body": "D2 [BLACK] — TEXTURE_LANGUAGE_R01 durable update\n\nEXACT HEAD = `2b0438cb817d41e53bec23944af7237893e12b4b`\nBASE MAIN OBSERVED = `b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1`\nSCOPE = VISUAL LANGUAGE / TEXTURE ANALYSIS ONLY\nIMAGE GENERATION = NO\nCUSTOM CODE = NO\nCUSTOM GLUE = NO\nPRODUCTION/CANON MUTATION = NO\n\n## Fresh CI on exact HEAD\n\n- `zorr-draw-qc-r01` run `33322667509` = SUCCESS\n- `hq-validate` run `33322667540` = SUCCESS\n- `oss-security` run `33322667519` = SUCCESS\n\nThis proves CI only for the exact documentation/evidence HEAD above; it does not promote production/canon or prove TEXTURE_LANGUAGE_R01.\n\n## Texture findings now recorded\n\n1. `C00-B` remains valuable for skull/jaw/yaw/ear/hair topology, but is rejected as an absolute texture-density master. Existing R02 semantic-face measurements are internally consistent across views yet outside #199 absolute character envelopes (7–8 tone bands; ~20–22% strong-edge density; ~5.9–7.1% deep ink; line hierarchy ~2.67–2.93). Therefore `TRANSFER CONSISTENCY PASS != ABSOLUTE STYLE PASS`.\n\n2. Existing `T05_B_BALANCED_SELECTED` was recovered and integrity-checked. It is retained as a close-up/head SCALE-BUDGET midpoint only: moderate source high-frequency amplitude, explicitly reducing further at full-body scale. It is NOT a material-semantic texture law.\n\n3. Refined model: `TEXTURE = SCALE_BUDGET x MATERIAL_RESPONSE`.\n   - CLOSE/HEAD: moderate structural micro may survive.\n   - MID: most micro collapses; material-defining meso remains.\n   - FULL BODY/FAR: macro form + structural edges + identity-critical accents.\n   - Material response remains separate: skin planes/scars; hair black mass/clusters; ivory cloth seams/tension folds; black cloth mass/few folds; leather broad specular; gold/silver focal islands; organic marks follow anatomy/flow.\n\n4. Existing ZORR/OpenCV path was audited, not modified. OpenCV 4.14.0 upstream primitives already cover current Sobel/Gaussian/Laplacian/K-means operations. No replacement/custom algorithm was written.\n\n5. Mature OSS candidate G'MIC was audited read-only: ready-made gradient/Sobel, frequency split/detail split, and quantization capabilities can cover future no-custom-code texture analysis. Current runtime does not provide a G'MIC CLI, so `GMIC_PHYSICAL_USE = NOT PROVEN` and no substitute implementation was written.\n\n## Exact blockers / next legal action\n\nPer-material numeric texture envelopes for C00-A/C/D remain `NOT PROVEN`: existing branch evidence does not contain semantic material masks, and writing a new extractor/wrapper is forbidden by OWNER. This is recorded as a bounded evidence gap, not filled by inference.\n\nCurrent terminal state:\n\n- `TEXTURE_TRANSFER_MATRIX_R01 = UPDATED / PROVISIONAL`\n- `EXACT_HEAD_CI = PASS`\n- `C00-B_TEXTURE_AUTHORITY = REJECTED; GEOMETRY_ROLE_RETAINED`\n- `T05_B = SCALE-AWARE CLOSE-UP MIDPOINT / NOT MATERIAL LAW`\n- `TEXTURE_LANGUAGE_R01 = NOT PASS`\n- `PER_MATERIAL_NUMERIC_ENVELOPES = NOT PROVEN`\n- `IMAGE_GENERATION_REQUIRES_OWNER_COMMAND`\n- `CUSTOM_CODE_REQUIRED_BUT_FORBIDDEN` where no existing/native/mature-OSS path exists\n\nNext legal work: continue read-only material routing and mature-OSS availability/reuse research on existing assets; no image generation and no new code.",
